	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The paper used “Random Survival Forests,” described as a “robust, nonparametric machine learning algorithmic method,” to identify risk factors without prespecified parametric assumptions. Inputs were prelisting SRTR tabular variables. The analysis used bootstrap/out-of-bag internal validation, which is most consistent with cross-validation style internal validation. The study did not use SHAP/LIME. No separate feature-selection step was described; variables in the SRTR dataset at listing were analyzed directly. Explicit hyperparameter tuning was not reported.  ￼

